2. Purpose

The purpose of this procedure is to perform the Global Control Process (GCP) review for Belgium tax reclaim cases maintained within STAR. The control ensures reclaim statuses remain accurate, aged cases are identified and escalated, and all stakeholders provide timely updates to support effective reclaim processing and reporting.

The control is performed semi-annually and covers status validation, ageing analysis, stakeholder follow-up, processing backlog review, and status correction activities.

Control Methodology

The control utilizes two separate STAR reports:

1. A Primary Reclaim Population Report, which serves as the source population for the control and contains all reclaim records within scope, including records that may not have linked payment lines or beneficiary references.
2. A Detailed Tax Form User Report, which provides additional reclaim details such as beneficiary information, event details, and address information.

As the Detailed Tax Form User Report may not contain all records present in the Primary Reclaim Population Report, a reconciliation process must be performed to ensure population completeness before any control review activities commence.

